####################################################################
# metric_state_order.ttl — HAND-AUTHORED. NOT GENERATED.
#
# Direction and severity of each reported metric state, for CAT2a
# (representation/rules/cat2a_process_priority.dlog): an incoming alarm is
# redundant with an active one only if it deviates in the SAME direction
# and is NOT MORE SEVERE (agreed 2026-09-21) — a reversal (tachycardia ->
# asystole) or an escalation (severe bradycardia -> asystole) is new
# information, not overlap.
#
# Same pattern as priority_rank.ttl: a small, stable, hand-authored layer
# over closed schemes (metricValueState:*, metricRhythm:*) that
# vocab_generated.ttl mints mechanically. A state not listed here has no
# direction, so an alarm reporting it is never silenced by CAT2a and never
# silences one — add it here if a new state appears.
#
# The state is read inside the reporting alarm's own graph (see
# cat2a_process_priority.dlog, REPORTED STATE); that relies on no alarm
# editing another's graph — last-wins stays removed.
#
# mdapoc:deviationDirection / mdapoc:deviationSeverity are declared in
# mdapoc.ttl — POC terms for now, framework candidates (deferred, see
# FRAMEWORK/PLAN_alarm_management_module.md). Severity is comparable only
# within one direction; higher = further from normal.
####################################################################

@prefix mdapoc:           <https://w3id.org/mda/poc#> .
@prefix metricValueState: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-value-state/> .
@prefix metricRhythm:     <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-rhythm/> .
@prefix xsd:              <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

metricValueState:Decreased          mdapoc:deviationDirection "low"  ; mdapoc:deviationSeverity "1"^^xsd:integer .
metricValueState:SeverelyDecreased  mdapoc:deviationDirection "low"  ; mdapoc:deviationSeverity "2"^^xsd:integer .
metricRhythm:Absent                 mdapoc:deviationDirection "low"  ; mdapoc:deviationSeverity "3"^^xsd:integer .
metricValueState:Increased          mdapoc:deviationDirection "high" ; mdapoc:deviationSeverity "1"^^xsd:integer .
metricValueState:SeverelyIncreased  mdapoc:deviationDirection "high" ; mdapoc:deviationSeverity "2"^^xsd:integer .
